<section class="im-section im-wrap">
	<div class="im-prose">
		<h2>A page for a thing that has not happened</h2>
		<p>Which sounds thin until you write one: <strong>why it is on the list</strong>, <strong>what it takes</strong>, and <strong>what has to be true before it can be booked</strong>. The third is the useful one — it is the difference between a wish and a plan, and most lines on most bucket lists fail it.</p>
		<p>The stats row holds what is known: the date, the odds, the place. When it happens, the page becomes an <a href="/collections/experience/page/">experience page</a> and this one links to it — the row in the list goes from a ring to a tick and stays exactly where it was.</p>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Do not write it as if it has happened.</strong> Future tense, or the whole collection stops meaning anything.</li>
			<li><strong>One state widget in the rail.</strong> It is the fact the page is about.</li>
			<li><strong>Not every line needs a page.</strong> Six of the nine on the list are one sentence and should stay that way.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>
